## 🔥 The problem in one picture

Job boards are noisy. The same role is posted on three sites, salaries are missing or quoted in five currencies, and a keyword match tells you nothing about whether you are actually a fit. Engineering students and early-career developers are left guessing which skills are worth learning next.

Hire-Archy fixes the three parts of that guesswork:

| Problem | What Hire-Archy does |
| --- | --- |
| Duplicates and dead links | Cleans, fuzzy de-duplicates (similarity 0.90) and keeps only real HTTPS apply URLs |
| Missing or mixed-currency pay | Normalizes salary to annual USD, and flags every imputed figure as `estimated` |
| "Am I a fit?" | Scores each role against your CV with a transparent 50 / 35 / 15 formula and lists the skills you are missing |

## ✨ What you can do

### 🔎 Job Explorer

Search and filter every indexed role by category, region, engineering branch, work mode, experience level, minimum salary and skills. Sort by recent, salary or best fit for your CV. **Fetch Live Jobs** pulls fresh postings for your current filters on demand.

![Job Explorer: role cards with a circular match score, salary range and skill tags](docs/images/job-explorer.png)

### 📄 CV matching

Upload a PDF. Hire-Archy extracts the text, detects your skills against a 64-skill canonical dictionary, estimates your experience and builds an embedding. Every role then gets a match score from 0 to 100 with the semantic, skill and experience parts shown separately, so you can see why a role ranked where it did.

### 📊 Market Analytics

Skill demand next to what each skill pays, salary quartiles (P25, median, P75) by experience level and work mode, remote share, and the highest-paying skill in the index. With a CV loaded, it also ranks the skills you are missing by how often they appear in roles you already score 60 or higher on.

![Market Analytics: top skills by demand with mean salary, and salary quartiles by experience and work mode](docs/images/market-analytics.png)

### 🏗️ Engineering taxonomy

Not just software. Roles are classified into 7 engineering branches and 32 domains: Computer Science & IT, Mechanical, Civil & Structural, Electrical & Electronics, Chemical & Process, Aerospace & Automotive, and Industrial & Manufacturing.

### 🎨 Three themes

Blended Urban, Light and Midnight, switchable from the header.

## 🛰️ Where the jobs come from

All collectors live in [`backend/app/etl/live_sources.py`](backend/app/etl/live_sources.py) and run concurrently. A source that is rate limited or down is skipped; the others still complete the sync.

| Source | Coverage | Key needed? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Arbeitnow | Open listings, mainly Europe | No |
| Remotive | Remote roles, keyword searchable | No |
| Greenhouse | Public boards: Stripe, Cloudflare, Datadog, NVIDIA, Anduril, Rippling, Atlassian, Retool | No |
| Lever | Public boards: Tesla, Joby Aviation, Anduril, Zoox, Aurora, Samsara, Waymo, Brex | No |
| Adzuna | India, Singapore, Australia, UK, Germany, US. Capped at 8 calls per sync to protect quota | `ADZUNA_APP_ID`, `ADZUNA_APP_KEY` |
| Jooble | 16 regional hubs across India, APAC, Europe, North America and the Middle East | `JOOBLE_API_KEY` |

The app works with no keys at all. Adzuna and Jooble simply log that they are skipped.

## 🧪 How the matching works

```
match score = 0.50 × semantic similarity
            + 0.35 × skill similarity
            + 0.15 × experience alignment

skill similarity = 0.60 × TF-IDF cosine + 0.40 × canonical-skill Jaccard
```

- **Semantic:** cosine similarity between the CV embedding and the job embedding.
- **Skill:** TF-IDF cosine over the text, blended with the overlap between your canonical skills and the role's.
- **Experience:** how far your years of experience sit from the role's band (entry 0-2, mid 2-5, senior 5-8, lead 8-12).
- **Embeddings:** OpenAI `text-embedding-3-small` when `OPENAI_API_KEY` is set. Otherwise a deterministic local 1,536-dimension feature-hash vector, so everything still runs offline. The ETL logs a warning when it falls back.
- **Salary:** parsed to annual USD. A missing range is imputed from same-category, same-experience listings, otherwise from documented experience benchmarks, and the row is marked `salary_is_estimated`.

The formulas are documented in docstrings under [`backend/app/analytics/`](backend/app/analytics/), and `test_composite_match_score_uses_documented_50_35_15_weights` pins the weights.

