## 🚀 Quick start (Windows 11, PowerShell)

Needs Python 3.11+, [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), Node.js 20+ and [pnpm](https://pnpm.io/).

```powershell
git clone https://github.com/Sneha2804-codes/Hire-Archy.git
cd Hire-Archy
```

**1. Backend** (terminal 1)

```powershell
cd backend
uv sync --extra dev
Copy-Item .env.example .env
uv run alembic upgrade head
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

The API runs on `http://localhost:8000`, with interactive docs at `/docs`. SQLite is the default, so there is no database server to install.

**2. Frontend** (terminal 2)

```powershell
cd frontend
Copy-Item .env.example .env.local
pnpm install
pnpm dev
```

Open `http://localhost:3000`.

**3. Load real jobs**

Click **ETL Sync** in the header, or run a one-off collection from `backend/`:

```powershell
uv run python -m app.etl.run --limit 25
```

> [!NOTE]
> Adzuna and Jooble are optional. To enable them, add `ADZUNA_APP_ID`, `ADZUNA_APP_KEY` and `JOOBLE_API_KEY` to `backend/.env`. For OpenAI embeddings, set `OPENAI_API_KEY`. Playwright is optional and only used by the feed scrapers in `backend/app/etl/scraper.py`: `uv run playwright install chromium`.

<details>
<summary><b>Environment variables</b></summary>

| Variable | File | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `DATABASE_URL` | `backend/.env` | `sqlite+aiosqlite:///./hire_archy.db` | Database connection |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | `backend/.env` | empty | Real embeddings; local hash vectors otherwise |
| `ADZUNA_APP_ID`, `ADZUNA_APP_KEY` | `backend/.env` | unset | Enables Adzuna |
| `JOOBLE_API_KEY` | `backend/.env` | unset | Enables Jooble |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` | `frontend/.env.local` | `http://localhost:8000/api` | Where the frontend finds the API |

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Optional: Postgres and Redis with Docker</b></summary>

`docker-compose.yml` starts `pgvector/pgvector:pg16` and `redis:7-alpine` for anyone who wants to move off SQLite. The app does not require either.

```powershell
docker compose up -d
```

Then point `DATABASE_URL` at the Postgres container.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Offline demo data</b></summary>

`backend/scripts/seed_dataset.py` removes legacy synthetic demo rows (source `hire-archy-seed`) and never inserts fake listings. It also holds deterministic fixtures used by the unit tests.

```powershell
uv run python scripts/seed_dataset.py
```

</details>

## 🔌 API

| Method | Endpoint | What it does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/api/jobs` | List jobs. Filters: `q`, `category`, `region`, `engineering_branch`, `work_mode`, `experience_level`, `min_salary`, repeated `skills`, `profile_id`. Sort with `sort_by=recent\|salary\|match`. Paginate with `page` and `limit` (max 100) |
| `POST` | `/api/jobs/live-search` | Fetch fresh postings for the given filters, persist new ones and return them |
| `POST` | `/api/cv/upload` | Upload a PDF CV. Returns the stored candidate profile |
| `GET` | `/api/analytics/overview` | Skill demand, salary quartiles, volume by category and work mode. Add `profile_id` for skill-gap ROI |
| `GET` | `/api/taxonomy` | Engineering branches, domains and regions |
| `POST` | `/api/etl/run?limit=25` | Start a live sync as a background task |
| `GET` | `/api/etl/logs` | Recent sync counters: fetched, duplicates, invalid |

`sort_by=match` needs a `profile_id`, so upload a CV first.

